# Hamro3D Component Standards

Apply these rules to every `.vue` file — components, layouts, and pages.

## H3d Prefix Requirement

Every Hamro3D component must be prefixed with `H3d`:

```
H3dButton.vue          H3dCard.vue            H3dInput.vue
H3dNavbar.vue          H3dFooter.vue          H3dSideProfileNavbar.vue
H3dProductCard.vue     H3dProductGallery.vue  H3dCommissionForm.vue
H3dLogo.vue            H3dBadge.vue           H3dModal.vue
```

Nuxt auto-imports all components from `app/components/` — no manual imports needed.

## File Order: Script Before Template

Every `.vue` file follows this strict order — no exceptions:

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
// All logic here
</script>

<template>
  <!-- All markup here -->
</template>
```

- `<script setup lang="ts">` is always first
- `<template>` is always second
- `<style>` block is **never used** (see next rule)

## No `<style>` Blocks

Hamro3D has zero `<style>` blocks anywhere in the codebase. All styling uses Tailwind utility classes with `h3d-` tokens. If you find yourself needing a `<style>` block, you are doing one of these wrong things:

1. Using hardcoded hex colors instead of `h3d-` tokens
2. Writing component-specific CSS instead of utility classes
3. Trying to override a third-party library (use a wrapper component instead)

The only exception is a single inline `style` attribute for truly dynamic values that Tailwind cannot express (e.g., `style="height: calc(100vh - 64px)"`). Even then, prefer CSS variables over magic numbers.

## Tailwind-Only Styling with h3d- Tokens

All color, typography, spacing, and border values must use `h3d-` tokens:

```vue
<!-- Correct -->
<div class="bg-h3d-surface border border-h3d-border rounded-sm p-6">
  <h2 class="font-h3d-display text-2xl text-h3d-text">Piece Name</h2>
  <p class="font-h3d-body text-sm text-h3d-muted">Details</p>
</div>

<!-- Wrong — Tailwind defaults, hardcoded hex, no h3d- tokens -->
<div class="bg-gray-900 border border-gray-700 rounded-lg p-6">
  <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-white">Piece Name</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">Details</p>
</div>
```

**Banned classes:**
- `bg-white`, `bg-black`, `bg-gray-*`, `bg-slate-*`, `bg-zinc-*`
- `text-gray-*`, `text-slate-*`, `text-neutral-*`
- `border-gray-*`, `border-slate-*`
- `rounded-lg`, `rounded-xl`, `rounded-2xl`, `rounded-full` on cards or panels
- `font-serif`, `font-sans`, `font-mono` (use `font-h3d-*` instead)

## definePageMeta Placement

On every page file, `definePageMeta` must be the **first statement** in `<script setup>`:

```typescript
<script setup lang="ts">
// 1. ALWAYS FIRST — compiler macro
definePageMeta({
  layout: 'profile',    // 'default' | 'profile' | 'admin' | 'checkout'
})

// 2. SEO meta — always second on page files
useSeoMeta({
  title: 'My Orders · Hamro3D',
  description: 'View your handcrafted pieces and their current progress.',
})

// 3. Everything else below
const route = useRoute()
...
</script>
```

## useSeoMeta Requirement

Every page file (in `app/pages/`) must call `useSeoMeta()`. No exceptions.

```typescript
useSeoMeta({
  title: '[Page Title] · Hamro3D',
  description: '[145-160 chars, brand voice, warm copy]',
  ogTitle: '[Page Title] · Hamro3D',
  ogDescription: '[Social-optimized description]',
  ogImage: '/og/page-slug.jpg',
})
```

## Layout Declaration Pattern

| Page location | Layout |
|---|---|
| `app/pages/index.vue` | default (omit or explicit) |
| `app/pages/products/**` | default |
| `app/pages/commission.vue` | default |
| `app/pages/our-story.vue` | default |
| `app/pages/contact.vue` | default |
| `app/pages/auth.vue` | default |
| `app/pages/cart.vue` | profile |
| `app/pages/wishlist.vue` | profile |
| `app/pages/checkout.vue` | default (or checkout) |
| `app/pages/profile/**` | profile |
| `app/pages/admin/**` | admin |

## NuxtLink vs `<a>` Tag

- **Always** use `<NuxtLink>` for internal navigation
- **Always** use `<a href="..." target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">` for external links
- **Never** use `<a href="/products">` for internal routes — this causes full page reloads

```vue
<!-- Internal — always NuxtLink -->
<NuxtLink to="/products/42" class="...">View Piece</NuxtLink>

<!-- External — always <a> with rel -->
<a href="https://instagram.com/hamro3d" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
  Instagram
</a>

<!-- Wrong — never use <a> for internal links -->
<a href="/products/42">View Piece</a>
```

## Nested Route Sibling Pattern

**The sibling pattern is mandatory** for all list + detail page pairs. Nuxt's file-based routing treats `orders.vue` + `orders/[id].vue` as parent/child — this breaks navigation. Always use the sibling pattern:

```
app/pages/profile/orders/
├── index.vue    → /profile/orders       ← list (sibling)
└── [id].vue     → /profile/orders/:id   ← detail (sibling)

app/pages/admin/orders/
├── index.vue    → /admin/orders         ← list (sibling)
└── [id].vue     → /admin/orders/:id     ← detail (sibling)
```

**Never use:**
```
app/pages/profile/
├── orders.vue           ← becomes parent shell — requires <NuxtPage /> slot
└── orders/[id].vue      ← only renders inside orders.vue — never standalone
```

## Empty State Pattern

Every list page that can have zero items must implement a branded empty state:

```vue
<template v-if="items.length === 0">
  <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-6 py-24 text-center">
    <p class="font-h3d-display text-3xl text-h3d-text/60">
      Nothing here yet.
    </p>
    <p class="font-h3d-body text-sm text-h3d-muted max-w-xs">
      <!-- Warm, contextual copy — see hamro3d-copy-standards.mdc -->
    </p>
    <NuxtLink
      to="/products"
      class="font-h3d-body text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-h3d-accent hover:text-h3d-text transition-colors"
    >
      Explore our pieces
    </NuxtLink>
  </div>
</template>
```

## Status Badge Pattern

Status badges always use three token layers — never a single background color:

```vue
<span
  :class="[
    'inline-flex items-center border px-2 py-0.5',
    'text-2xs uppercase tracking-widest font-h3d-body rounded-sm',
    statusBadgeClass(item.status)
  ]"
>
  {{ item.status }}
</span>
```

```typescript
// Status-to-token mapping — always a dedicated helper function
function statusBadgeClass(status: MockUserOrderStatus): string {
  switch (status) {
    case 'Delivered':   return 'border-h3d-success/50 bg-h3d-success/10 text-h3d-success'
    case 'In Progress': return 'border-h3d-accent/50 bg-h3d-accent/10 text-h3d-accent'
    case 'Processing':  return 'border-h3d-border bg-h3d-base text-h3d-muted'
    case 'Cancelled':   return 'border-h3d-error/50 bg-h3d-error/10 text-h3d-error'
    default:            return 'border-h3d-border bg-h3d-base text-h3d-muted'
  }
}
```

## Form Accessibility Rules

```vue
<!-- Every form field must have an associated label -->
<label for="customer-name" class="font-h3d-body text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-h3d-muted">
  Your Name
</label>
<input
  id="customer-name"
  type="text"
  class="bg-h3d-surface border border-h3d-border text-h3d-text ..."
  aria-required="true"
/>

<!-- Icon-only buttons require aria-label -->
<button type="button" aria-label="Remove from wishlist" class="...">
  <svg .../>
</button>

<!-- Required field indicator — use aria-required, not just * -->
<input aria-required="true" ... />
```
